---
description: >
  Project-root brevity sweep — `.aide/intent.aide` is ~2,000 lines of paragraph-length outcomes, retired prior designs, type signatures, and exact strings that compound into the heaviest cascade of bloat in the tree. Wholesale rewrite required.
intent: >
  Audit the project root spec against the Brevity Contract. Every cap is
  exceeded by 5-15x and forbidden content saturates frontmatter and body.
  Most brain-layer doctrine duplicates what `src/.aide` and the brain-related
  submodule specs already say, so the rewrite is also a sibling-redundancy
  prune — push brain-layer narrative downward, leave the project root with
  only what every descendant truly inherits.
misalignment:
  - spec-bloat
  - spec-gap
---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is ~2,617 chars (cap 200) — a single paragraph enumerating
  the six body-section names, marker token vocabulary, the `(string | null)[]`
  type signature, the arg-index slot meaning for the bundled default, the
  `--brain` flag default, sentinel sentinels, and the install vs `/aide:brain config`
  partition. None of this belongs in `description`.
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (type signatures, exact strings, CLI flag enumerations, marker tokens)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `intent` is ~513 words (cap 100) and restates the description verbatim with
  added paragraphs about delegation flow, install behavior, and slot semantics.
  Trim to a single ten-second north-star paragraph naming what this repo is
  *for* — methodology authoring + MCP delivery — and let outcomes carry the rest.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 21 items (cap 4). Each outcome is a paragraph-length
  essay naming exact identifiers, type signatures, marker tokens, file paths,
  arg-index numbers, sentinel string lists, status enum membership counts, and
  framework-internal symbols (`provisionBrain`, `parseBrainAide`, `buildBrainState`,
  `interpolateArgs`, `obsidianBrainAideTemplate`, `writeMcpEntry`, etc.). Compress
  to 3-4 domain success criteria a QA agent could falsify against an output
  artifact, not against compiler/test-level invariants.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + outcomes-purpose test (most items are code-level invariants the type system enforces)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 16+ items, all paragraph-length, almost all citing
  retired prior-design names (`<BRAIN_PATH>`, `__UNWIRED__`, `PATH_SLOT_INDEX`,
  `resolveBrainRoot`, `argSlots`, `connector`, `rootPath`, `entryFile`, `tools`,
  `Hub`-suffix, the four-vs-five state vocabulary, etc.). Migration history and
  retired prior designs are forbidden content. These belong in git history,
  PR descriptions, or CHANGELOG, not in a durable spec.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (migration history, retired prior designs)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Context` is ~1,000+ words (cap ~150) and explains the entire brain-layer
  architecture — six body sections, live-vs-seed split, arg-index slot semantics,
  null-as-unwired-signal, four-state vocabulary, sync-as-only-mutation, drift
  semantics, storage-agnostic vocabulary. This is implementation-contract material
  at best.
  Traces to: `## Context` | Brevity Contract cap (~150 words)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 14+ paragraph-length decisions (cap ~5, ≤80 words each).
  Most encode implementation contracts — marker token format, the closed `kind`
  enum, `provisionBrain`'s two-step pipeline shape, the `aide_init` conditional
  flip — that belong in `plan.aide` or in code. The Strategy-exceeds-5-decisions
  rule is the explicit signal to **split this scope into child specs**: brain-layer
  doctrine should live under a dedicated child spec, not at the project root.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + "split, don't expand" rule
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` together carry 20+ scenarios with
  embedded YAML/JSON code blocks, exact marker strings, exact path enumerations
  (`coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md`, `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`,
  `coding-playbook/update-playbook.md`, `research/research.md`), exact slot index
  numbers, full body-section example bytes for the bundled obsidian template.
  Caps are 2-3 brief examples each; forbidden content rule forbids exact strings,
  file paths, and format tokens.
  Traces to: `## Good examples`, `## Bad examples` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## References` has one ~600-word bullet plus 8 more paragraph-length bullets
  that repeat rationale across every sibling spec. Per the contract, a `## References`
  bullet is "path + one-line description of what was drawn." This section as
  written is half the size of a small spec.
  Traces to: `## References` | Brevity Contract format
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] Sibling redundancy: most brain-layer content here (six-section grammar,
  YAML-null-as-unwired-slot signal, four-state vocabulary, `--brain` flag
  semantics, `cli/init` no-brain-wiring contract, `cli/sync` null-refusal,
  arg-index slot semantics) is repeated nearly verbatim in `src/.aide`,
  `src/cli/init/.aide`, `src/cli/sync/.aide`, `src/service/buildBrainState/.aide`,
  `src/service/install/provisionBrain/.aide`, `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide`,
  and `src/tools/brain/.aide`. The parent re-explains everything every child
  also explains. Pick one home for each invariant (brain-layer doctrine probably
  lives under a dedicated brain-layer parent), prune the rest from this root.
  Traces to: `outcomes`, `## Strategy`, `## Bad examples` | Brevity Contract sibling-redundancy doctrine
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] Carry-forward from prior alignment cycle (still relevant after the rewrite):
  outcomes restate brain.aide methodology-doc commitments that the doc at
  `.aide/docs/brain-aide.md` did not initially track. Verify the doc still matches
  the rewritten root after this brevity sweep lands; the per-rewrite re-walk is
  what closes the doc-drift cascade flagged in `feedback_methodology_doc_must_match_root.md`.
  Traces to: outcome about brain-aide.md doc existence + methodology-doc cascade
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [ ] `.aide/handoff.aide` — entire 527-line file is forbidden content (state
  summary, "where this cycle stopped", anti-regression invariants enumerating
  retired designs, what-the-next-agent-must-do, open questions). It has no
  `scope`/`description`/`intent`/`outcomes` frontmatter; it is a session-state
  artifact. Per the methodology, pipeline-state-during-rework belongs in
  `session.aide` (added explicitly for this case) or in git history. Recommend
  retiring the file: promote durable architectural commitments into the rewritten
  root and brain-layer specs; promote retros to the brain at `process/retro/`;
  delete the file so future readers don't treat it as durable intent.
  Traces to: file existence, frontmatter, every body section | Forbidden content (migration history, retired prior designs, pipeline-state commentary)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content (entire file)

### `.aide/readme.aide` brevity findings

- [ ] `.aide/readme.aide` `outcomes.desired` has 5 items (cap 4); items are
  paragraph length and item 0 enumerates exact MCP client names (Claude Code,
  Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code/Copilot, Windsurf), exact JSON root keys
  (`mcpServers`, `servers`), and the `@latest` version-pin convention. Per
  the contract, exact strings, CLI flag enumerations, and per-client config
  details are forbidden. Outcome should commit to "the README delivers a
  copy-pasteable config for every supported client without translation"
  without naming the clients.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (exact strings, CLI/config enumerations)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `.aide/readme.aide` `outcomes.undesired` has 6 paragraph-length items
  enumerating retired/forbidden specifics (`details/summary` HTML, bare
  package names without `@latest`, PATH-troubleshooting omission). Compress
  to 3-4 falsifiable failure-mode bullets.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `.aide/readme.aide` `## Context` lines 81-83 hardcodes the tool roster
  ("the server currently ships a small set of tools (`aide_discover`, `aide_read`,
  `aide_scaffold`, `aide_validate`, `aide_inspect`, `aide_info`, `aide_init`,
  `aide_upgrade`, `aide_brain`)") and a count-derived feasibility argument.
  Both are forbidden — count-pinning and roster enumeration are the same drift
  pattern flagged in `src/.aide`'s carry-forward issue. Removing the count and
  roster from the README spec's reasoning closes the cascade.
  Traces to: `## Context` | Forbidden content (CLI/MCP tool name enumerations) + spec-gap (cascading from src/.aide undesired outcomes against count-pinning)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat, spec-gap
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `.aide/readme.aide` `## Strategy` enumerates ~12 paragraph-length decisions
  including specific badge URLs, specific section ordering rules, specific
  per-client config snippets, exact npx flag combinations (`-y`, `@latest`),
  PATH-troubleshooting recipes. Cap is ~5 decisions ≤80 words each. Strategy
  should hold the why-this-shape decisions; the what-each-section-must-contain
  belongs in code or in a README template.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `.aide/readme.aide` `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce
  full markdown READMEs verbatim with exact JSON config blocks, exact bash
  commands, exact badge image URLs, exact tool-doc Markdown. Per the contract,
  examples should be brief and pattern-illustrative, not byte-faithful
  templates. The README itself is the right home for these literals; the spec
  documents the shape, not the contents.
  Traces to: `## Good examples`, `## Bad examples` | Forbidden content (exact strings, exact JSON shapes)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Carry-forward: prior cycle flagged Quick Start npx command missing
  `@latest` (plan-gap) and Context lines 81-83 hardcoding stale six-tool count
  (spec-gap). The bloat sweep above subsumes the spec-gap by removing the
  enumeration entirely. The `@latest` plan-gap is a downstream effect of the
  spec being too prescriptive — the spec should commit to the version-pinning
  invariant once and let the plan apply it consistently across surfaces.
  Traces to: README.md Quick Start | Misalignment: plan-gap (subsumed by removing exact-CLI-string from spec)

## Retro

This spec was written by treating the project root as the place where every
invariant must be restated *for safety*. The result exemplifies every
anti-pattern the Brevity Contract was added to forbid — paragraph-length
description, paragraph-length outcomes, retired-prior-design enumerations,
exact strings, type signatures, arg-index numbers, file path enumerations,
marker tokens — and a cascade where every descendant spec restates the parent.

The bloat traces to the spec-writer not enforcing caps mid-interview and not
suggesting child-spec decomposition for the brain layer. The strategist
compounded it by encoding pipeline-mechanism decisions in Strategy paragraphs
instead of leaving them in `plan.aide`. The aligner role was missing entirely.

Recommended sequence: **wholesale rewrite, top-down**. Root first, then push
the brain-layer narrative down into a single child spec and let `src/.aide`
and the brain-related leaves prune their restatements. The project's actual
root commitments are smaller than this spec admits: methodology authoring as
the single source of truth, two MCP delivery channels (handshake + install),
and progressive disclosure as the delivery shape. Everything else cascades.
